689 0 obj
<<
/Author (Codruta Elena Ciurescu\054 Lorena Dima\054 Vlad Alexandru Ciurescu\054 Gratiela Georgiana Noja\054 Alin Viorel Istodor\054 Marius Alexandru Moga\054 Lavinia Cosmina Ardelean\054 Laura\055Cristina Rusu and Marius Traian Leretter)
/CreationDate (D\07220240306171839\05308\04700\047)
/Creator (LaTeX with hyperref)
/Keywords (periodontitis\073 laser therapy\073 Er\054Cr\072YSGG\073 Gaussian graphical models\073 structural equation modeling\073 network analysis\073 non\055surgical periodontal therapy\073 periodontal pocket depth\073 clinical attachment level\073 bleeding on probing)
/ModDate (D\07220240306102300\05301\04700\047)
/Producer (pdfTeX\0551\05640\05621)
/Subject (Background and Objectives\072 This paper aims to assess the role of laser therapy in periodontitis through an innovative approach involving computational prediction and advanced modeling performed through network analysis \050Gaussian graphical models\204GGMs\051 and structural equations \050SEM\051\056 Materials and Methods\072 Forty patients\054 exhibiting periodontal pockets with a minimum depth of 5 mm\054 were randomly divided into two groups\072 a control group and a laser group\056 Four specific indicators were measured for each tooth\054 namely periodontal pocket depth \050PPD\051\054 clinical attachment level \050CAL\051\054 bleeding on probing \050BOP\051\054 and plaque index \050PI\051\054 and the mean of six measured values was recorded at five time markers \050baseline\054 6 months\054 1 year\054 2 years\054 and 4 years\051\056 The assessment algorithm included enrollment\054 measurements\054 and differential non\055surgical periodontal treatment\054 according to the group allocation\056 Scaling\054 root planing\054 and chlorhexidine 1\045 were conducted for the control group\054 and scaling\054 root planing and erbium\054 chromium\072yttrium\055scandium\055gallium\055garnet \050Er\054CR\072YSGG\051 laser therapy were conducted for the laser group\056 Results\072 The main results highlight that the addition of laser treatment to scaling and root planing led to notable clinical improvements\054 decreasing the PPD values\054 reducing the BOP scores\054 and increasing the CAL\056 Conclusions\072 Notable relationships between the specific indicators considered were highlighted by both the GGMs and by SEM\054 thus confirming their suitability as proxies for the success of periodontal treatment\056)
/Title (Laser Therapy Effects on Periodontal Status\072 A Randomized Study Using Gaussian Network Analysis and Structural Equation Modeling Approach)
>>
endobj
